coder › Implemented `retry` in `src/retry.ts` and added `src/retry.test.ts`.

What changed:
- `src/retry.ts`
  - `retry` now validates `attempts < 1` and throws a `RangeError` before `fn` runs.
  - Calls `fn` up to `attempts` times, returning the first successful result.
  - Between failures it awaits the provided `sleep`, starting at `baseMs` and doubling each time.
  - `sleep` defaults to a real `setTimeout`-backed wait when not provided.
  - After the last failure it throws `Error` with message `gave up after N attempts: <last error message>` and `cause` set to the last error.

- `src/retry.test.ts`
  - Success on first call, no sleep recorded.
  - Retry with failures at `attempts: 4`, recording waits `[5, 10, 20]`.
  - Final-failure error message and `cause`.
  - `attempts: 0` throws `RangeError` and `fn` is never called.
  - Default `setTimeout` sleep actually waits (~20ms measured).

